From: prokrypt <prokrypt@edited.us>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:13:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pinebook-pro: let SPL load U-Boot and TF-A from the SD card
 first

SPL looked for the U-Boot FIT (U-Boot + TF-A) on the boot device it was
loaded from first, so booting from SPI it always used the FIT in the
flash. Try the SD card first (FIT at sector 0x4000, 8 MB in), then SPI,
then the eMMC. A card without a FIT there (all zeros before its first
partition) fails the image check and SPL goes on to the SPI flash as
before.

This lets a test TF-A (and U-Boot) be booted by writing a FIT to an SD
card, with the proven one in SPI as the fallback: pull the card, or zero
those sectors, and the next boot uses the flash again. Only TPL and SPL
stay fixed in SPI.
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
index 240f8b35..63cab749 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 
 / {
 	chosen {
-		u-boot,spl-boot-order = "same-as-spl", &sdhci, &spiflash, &sdmmc;
+		u-boot,spl-boot-order = &sdmmc, &spiflash, &sdhci;
 	};
 
 	config {
